  "necessity_paragraph": "The patient presents with recurrent episodes of palpitations, lightheadedness, and intermittent syncope suggestive of paroxysmal atrial fibrillation and sick sinus syndrome, corresponding to diagnosis codes I49.5 and I48.0. Given the personal history of transient ischemic attack and cerebral infarction, continuous mobile cardiac telemetry is ordered to detect arrhythmic events and guide appropriate anticoagulation and rate-control management. This service is medically necessary to detect the arrhythmic events indicated in the clinical note and to support the management of the documented diagnoses."
